knext bundled fix for vinext 1.1.0 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3753
What it fixes: next/dynamic's server render put the preload hints (`<link rel="modulepreload">`, hoisted into <head>) in front of the Suspense boundary. A hoisted link that follows a text node makes React's SSR write a `<!-- -->` text separator, so text followed by a dynamic() component rendered `Index<!-- --><!--$-->1<!--/$-->` instead of Next.js's `Index<!--$-->1<!--/$-->` (Next.js deploy test test/e2e/next-dynamic). The hints now render as the boundary's first child, next to the lazy component, as Next.js renders <PreloadChunks>; React still hoists them.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3753.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.1.0 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

--- a/dist/shims/dynamic.js
+++ b/dist/shims/dynamic.js
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@
 					resetKey: 0
 				}, lazyElement);
 			}
-			return React.createElement(React.Fragment, null, React.createElement(DynamicPreloadChunks, { moduleIds: preloadModuleIds }), React.createElement(React.Suspense, { fallback }, content));
+			return React.createElement(React.Suspense, { fallback }, React.createElement(DynamicPreloadChunks, { moduleIds: preloadModuleIds }), content);
 		};
 		ServerDynamic.displayName = "DynamicServer";
 		return ServerDynamic;
